<p>
<H2> Other_Examples </H2>
 
Let us look at a few examples where Krawtchouk polynomials
appear quite naturally.
 
<p>
<h4> Random_walk </h4>
 
The following three examples do not exemplify the Krawtchouk polynomials
directly, but lead to them as solutions of the problems.  As shown
later, they all are actually paraphrase of the same idea.
  
Consider one-dimensional random walk of finite step size (1) on a grid
of integers.  Say, a step is made  every second.  After n seconds the
drunker, who made in total i steps ahead and j steps backwards
(clearly n=i+j) is located in position x=i-j.  Notice that as before
there are two sets of variables that are natural in the drunker
space-time (see Figure ....) and which determine the space time
location (event):  regular coordinates of space and time \{x,n\}, and
isotropic variables \{i,j\}, with the obvious coordinate-change rules:
<p>
\cases{ x =<td align=right> i-j </tr>
<tr><td align=right>\cr        n =<td align=right> i+j </tr>
</table>  \textrm{\qquad  and  \qquad}\cases{ i =<td align=right> {1 \over 2} (n-j) </tr>
<tr><td align=right>\cr        j =<td align=right> {1 \over 2} (n+j) </tr>
</table><p>
Analogy with space-time of relativity theory is clear: ...  determine
the max speed possible, ``light cone''.
<p>
<h4> Urn_model_(or_mathematics_of<sub> \it_I_Ching </sub>) </h4>
 
Suppose you have an urn that contains n balls of two sorts: blue and
red. Suppose that every minute one ball changes its color (Feinsilver's
Demon draws randomly a ball, repaints it, and locates back in the urn).
The question is what states are stable in this process.
<p>
\begin{quotation}Comment: This is Western paraphrase of the ancient Chinese divination
philosophical formal system of <i> I Ching</i> where all situations are
modeled into 64 hexagrams, each consisting of six lines. A line may be
whole or broken, representing principle Yang or In, respectively.  The
story of the Universe, or development of a real situation is believed to
consist of mutual changes of particular line of a current hexagram
between these two states.
\end{quotation}
